HST Office: compact ribbon (Ctrl+F1) with a quick command row; the document tab strip is 32 px high.

1.0.2 ribbon (owner decisions 14/11/2026, gap list G07 and G13, mockup v2):
- Ctrl+F1, a double-click on a tab or the chevron at the lower right end of the ribbon (˄) collapse the
  Tabbed ribbon of Writer, Sheets, Slides and Draw to 80 logical px: the tab row and a row of the current
  tab's main commands with their own toolbar controllers (data/ribbon/quick-rows.json, generated into
  sfx2/source/notebookbar/HstRibbonQuickRows.hxx by scripts/patches/generate-ribbon-quick-rows.py; each
  app's rows hold only commands of that app's own ribbon). The banner (260 x 75) stands across both rows;
  the tab row's search box and menu button stop before it (NotebookbarTabControlBase::HstSetRowReserve).
- Choosing a tab of the compact ribbon (click, access key) drops its full page over the document, below
  the tab row and left of the banner (vcl/source/control/HstRibbonDrop.cxx); Esc, a click outside or a
  command run from it closes it. Ctrl+F1, the quick row's ˅ chevron or a double-click on a tab restore
  the full ribbon, as does the ≡ menu's "Collapse the Ribbon / Show the Full Ribbon (Ctrl+F1)" entry. Each
  app remembers its state (HSTRibbon/CompactApps).
- The tab control's page rectangle stops before the banner (TabControl::ImplHstPageReserve,
  NotebookbarTabControlBase::HstSetPageReserve), set before each allocation: a page is never laid out at
  the full width first and then narrowed after a posted event, which showed the groups in a wider state for
  a moment on tab and document switches. A page shown in the popup is left to the popup.
- framework DocumentTabBar: 32 px high (G13), at least the text height and its padding.
- Strings: STR_HST_RIBBON_COLLAPSE / STR_HST_RIBBON_EXPAND with their Vietnamese translation.

